      "text": "## Skin Layers: Three Zones"
    },
    {
      "id": "10-INTEGUMENTARY.md#006",
      "path": [
        "10-INTEGUMENTARY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:human-biology:10-integumentary, git-history:human-biology:10-integumentary]",
        "canonical_path": "human-biology/10-INTEGUMENTARY.md",
        "concepts": "[integumentary]",
        "current_path": "human-biology/10-INTEGUMENTARY.md",
        "id": "maxim:human-biology:integumentary",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "human-biology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[integumentary]",
        "section": "human-biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Integumentary System",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nSURFACE\n  │\n  ├── EPIDERMIS (~0.1–0.2 mm; up to 1.5 mm on palms/soles)\n  │   Avascular — nutrients via diffusion from dermis\n  │   Stratified squamous epithelium\n  │   4–5 layers (strata) from deep to superficial:\n  │\n  ├── DERMIS (~1–4 mm)\n  │   Vascular, sensory receptors, hair follicles, glands\n  │   Collagen (type I + III) + elastin framework\n  │\n  └── HYPODERMIS (subcutaneous fat)\n      Adipocytes + loose CT\n      Thermal insulation, energy storage, cushioning\n      NOT part of skin proper (not \"integumentary\" sensu stricto, but contiguous)\n```"
    },
