      },
      "text": "From basement membrane to surface (keratinocyte maturational sequence):"
    },
    {
      "id": "10-INTEGUMENTARY.md#010",
      "path": [
        "10-INTEGUMENTARY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:human-biology:10-integumentary, git-history:human-biology:10-integumentary]",
        "canonical_path": "human-biology/10-INTEGUMENTARY.md",
        "concepts": "[integumentary]",
        "current_path": "human-biology/10-INTEGUMENTARY.md",
        "id": "maxim:human-biology:integumentary",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "human-biology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[integumentary]",
        "section": "human-biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Integumentary System",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nSTRATUM BASALE (deepest — proliferative layer):\n  Columnar cells on basement membrane (laminin + type IV collagen)\n  Keratinocyte stem cells: divide → push daughter cells upward\n  Also contains: melanocytes, Merkel cells"
    },
    {
      "id": "10-INTEGUMENTARY.md#011",
      "path": [
        "10-INTEGUMENTARY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:human-biology:10-integumentary, git-history:human-biology:10-integumentary]",
        "canonical_path": "human-biology/10-INTEGUMENTARY.md",
        "concepts": "[integumentary]",
        "current_path": "human-biology/10-INTEGUMENTARY.md",
        "id": "maxim:human-biology:integumentary",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "human-biology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[integumentary]",
        "section": "human-biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Integumentary System",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "STRATUM SPINOSUM (\"prickle cell layer\"):\n  Several cells thick; cells connected by DESMOSOMES (intercellular bridges — \"spines\")\n  Active keratin synthesis\n  Langerhans cells interspersed"
    },
    {
      "id": "10-INTEGUMENTARY.md#012",
      "path": [
        "10-INTEGUMENTARY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:human-biology:10-integumentary, git-history:human-biology:10-integumentary]",
        "canonical_path": "human-biology/10-INTEGUMENTARY.md",
        "concepts": "[integumentary]",
        "current_path": "human-biology/10-INTEGUMENTARY.md",
        "id": "maxim:human-biology:integumentary",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "human-biology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[integumentary]",
        "section": "human-biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Integumentary System",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "STRATUM GRANULOSUM:\n  2–3 layers; cells contain KERATOHYALIN GRANULES (profilaggrin → filaggrin)\n  LAMELLAR BODIES (membrane-coating granules): lipid-rich vesicles\n  → exocytose at granular–cornified junction → form lipid bilayers of stratum corneum"
    },
    {
      "id": "10-INTEGUMENTARY.md#013",
      "path": [
        "10-INTEGUMENTARY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:human-biology:10-integumentary, git-history:human-biology:10-integumentary]",
        "canonical_path": "human-biology/10-INTEGUMENTARY.md",
        "concepts": "[integumentary]",
        "current_path": "human-biology/10-INTEGUMENTARY.md",
        "id": "maxim:human-biology:integumentary",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "human-biology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[integumentary]",
        "section": "human-biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Integumentary System",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "STRATUM LUCIDUM (only in thick skin: palms + soles):\n  Translucent, no nuclei, densely packed eleidin (intermediate keratin form)"
    },
    {
      "id": "10-INTEGUMENTARY.md#014",
      "path": [
        "10-INTEGUMENTARY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:human-biology:10-integumentary, git-history:human-biology:10-integumentary]",
        "canonical_path": "human-biology/10-INTEGUMENTARY.md",
        "concepts": "[integumentary]",
        "current_path": "human-biology/10-INTEGUMENTARY.md",
        "id": "maxim:human-biology:integumentary",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "human-biology",
