        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[integumentary]",
        "section": "human-biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Integumentary System",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "STRATUM CORNEUM (outermost, 15–20 layers):\n  Dead, anucleate, fully keratinized \"corneocytes\"\n  Surrounded by lipid bilayers (ceramides + free FA + cholesterol) → \"brick and mortar\"\n  → Barrier function: limits water loss + excludes hydrophilic molecules\n  Continuously shed (desquamation): full epidermal turnover ~28–45 days\n```"
    },
