      "text": "## Cell Types in Epidermis"
    },
    {
      "id": "10-INTEGUMENTARY.md#017",
      "path": [
        "10-INTEGUMENTARY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:human-biology:10-integumentary, git-history:human-biology:10-integumentary]",
        "canonical_path": "human-biology/10-INTEGUMENTARY.md",
        "concepts": "[integumentary]",
        "current_path": "human-biology/10-INTEGUMENTARY.md",
        "id": "maxim:human-biology:integumentary",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "human-biology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[integumentary]",
        "section": "human-biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Integumentary System",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "| Cell | % of epidermis | Origin | Function |\n|------|---------------|--------|----------|\n| Keratinocytes | ~90% | Ectoderm | Produce keratin; terminal differentiation → barrier |\n| Melanocytes | ~5–10% | Neural crest | Synthesize melanin (eumelanin = brown/black; pheomelanin = red/yellow); transfer melanosomes to keratinocytes; UV protection |\n| Langerhans cells | ~3–5% | Bone marrow (monocyte lineage) | Antigen-presenting cells (DC type); migrate to lymph nodes on activation; first immune response line |\n| Merkel cells | < 1% | Neural crest (or epidermal progenitor) | Mechanoreceptors for light touch; synapse with nerve endings; Merkel cell carcinoma (rare, aggressive) |"
    },
